---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="A Legacy of Blessed Contentment"
  description="A eulogy reflecting on the life of Baruch Asher, a grandfather who embodied both blessed self-sufficiency and the pursuit of happiness."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 sm:py-16">
    <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <header class="text-center space-y-6 mb-12">
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center space-y-4">
          <a 
            href="/writings" 
            class="inline-flex items-center text-accent dark:text-accent-dark hover:text-accent-hover dark:hover:text-accent-hover font-medium transition-colors"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-1" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
            </svg>
            Back to Writings
          </a>
          <div class="flex items-center text-sm text-secondary-light dark:text-secondary-dark space-x-2">
            <time datetime="2024-03-11">March 11, 2024</time>
            <span>•</span>
            <span>Eulogy</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-primary-light dark:text-primary-dark leading-tight">
          A Legacy of Blessed Contentment
        </h1>
        
        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-secondary-light dark:text-secondary-dark max-w-3xl mx-auto italic">
          In memory of Baruch Asher — a grandfather who embodied both blessed self-sufficiency and the pursuit of happiness.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:text-primary-light dark:prose-headings:text-primary-dark prose-p:text-secondary-light dark:prose-p:text-secondary-dark prose-blockquote:text-accent dark:prose-blockquote:text-accent-dark">
        <p class="lead text-xl font-medium text-primary-light dark:text-primary-dark">
          Same BS different day. Zeydie would always start conversations with his familiar line — it's another day, thankful to be alive. I'm just one day older, he said — 2 weeks ago on his 89th birthday.
        </p>

        <p>
          Today is not just another day. Today we come together to celebrate the life of a man who raised a beautiful family and left a legacy that will live on.
        </p>

        <p>
          Over the past couple of days, I have been reflecting on my grandpa and on his Hebrew name - Baruch Asher - Blessed Contentment.
        </p>

        <h2>Baruch — Blessed Self-Sufficiency</h2>
        <p>
          The term Baruch - blessed - is also attributed to God and can mean self-sufficient. I would proudly say to Zeydie - you really were an entrepreneur - establishing a reputable business, being the go-to source for commercial laundry for the top hotels, airlines, and beyond. I don't know. He would say. His humility would not allow him to gloat in his achievements, but we are certainly proud of his go-getter attitude, his self sufficient character, and his business acumen.
        </p>

        <h2>Asher — The Pursuit of Happiness</h2>
        <p>
          Asher - means happy or content - Rabbi Shamshon Rafael Hirsch notes that the term (in connection to the name of the son of Jacob) bespeaks the characteristic of being in a state of seeking happiness. Of looking for moment or opportunity to achieve happiness and contentment. Zeydie was always basking and delighting in those happy moments in his life - in his beautiful relationship with our beloved Bubbie, in seeing his grand and great grand kids, in just living his life.
        </p>

        <h2>A Mind That Never Settled</h2>
        <p>
          He was never satisfied with superficialities. As Aaron and I were becoming religious he would always push us, asking us questions to dig deeper and not to take anything for granted. I pity all of the missionaries that knocked on his door and thought he would be an easy convert.
        </p>

        <h2>A Heart Full of Joy</h2>
        <p>
          He always had a smile on his face and a twinkle in his eye (not the glass one). He was a master shmoozer and a brilliant storyteller.
        </p>

        <h2>Cherished by All</h2>
        <p>
          Aviya and Tzofia loved zeydie and always enjoyed singing and chatting with him and they will miss him greatly!
        </p>

        <p>
          Georgia was just as comfortable spending time at their home as she would be with her own grandparents. She felt very welcome and loved at his and bubbies home.
        </p>

        <p>
          They ran a home of love and clearly cherished their family.
        </p>

        <h2>A Legacy to Follow</h2>
        <p>
          May we all learn from his example - living lives in which we strive and struggle to put in the effort and to seek moments of joy and happiness.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent dark:border-accent-dark pl-6 py-2 my-8 bg-card-bg-light/50 dark:bg-card-bg-dark/50 rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-lg font-medium text-primary-light dark:text-primary-dark">
            May we all learn from his example — living lives in which we strive and struggle to put in the effort and to seek moments of joy and happiness.
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2>The Promise of Tomorrow</h2>
        <p>
          And may God fulfill prophecy in Isaiah:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-card-bg-light dark:bg-card-bg-dark border border-border-light dark:border-border-dark rounded-xl p-6 my-8 text-center">
          <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-primary-light dark:text-primary-dark mb-4" dir="rtl" style="font-family: 'SBL Hebrew', 'Times New Roman', serif;">
            בִּלַּ֤ע הַמָּ֙וֶת֙ לָנֶ֔צַח וּמָחָ֨ה אֲדֹנָ֧י יְהוִ֛ה דִּמְעָ֖ה מֵעַ֣ל כָּל־פָּנִ֑ים וְחֶרְפַּ֣ת עַמֹּ֗ו יָסִיר֙ מֵעַ֣ל כָּל־הָאָ֔רֶץ כִּ֥י יְהוָ֖ה דִּבֵּֽר׃ פ
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-secondary-light dark:text-secondary-dark italic">
            He has concealed death forever, and the Lord God shall wipe the tears off every face, and the shame of His people He shall remove from upon the entire earth, for the Lord has spoken.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <footer class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-border-light dark:border-border-dark">
        <div class="text-center space-y-4">
          <a 
            href="/writings" 
            class="inline-flex items-center text-accent dark:text-accent-dark hover:text-accent-hover dark:hover:text-accent-hover font-medium transition-colors"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-1" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
            </svg>
            Back to Writings
          </a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </main>

  <style>
    .prose {
      @apply text-secondary-light dark:text-secondary-dark;
    }
    
    .prose h2, .prose h3 {
      @apply text-primary-light dark:text-primary-dark font-bold mt-8 mb-4;
    }
    
    .prose p {
      @apply mb-6 leading-relaxed;
    }
    
    .prose blockquote {
      @apply border-l-4 border-accent dark:border-accent-dark pl-6 py-2 my-8 italic;
    }
    
    .lead {
      @apply text-xl font-medium text-primary-light dark:text-primary-dark mb-8;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
